        <headline>Marine Weather Statement issued September 26 at 10:02AM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>The areas affected include...

Central Long Island Sound...

At 958 AM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms. These
thunderstorms were located along a line extending from Central Long
Island Sound to Great South Bay, moving west at 25 knots.

There is already a gale warning in effect so wind gusts up to 45 kt
can be expected.

Locations impacted include...
Falkner Island, Mouth of the Housatonic River, Smithtown Bay, Central
Long Island Sound, Herod Point, Port Jefferson Harbor, Stratford
Shoal, and Bridgeport.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners can expect gale force winds, locally higher waves,
lightning strikes, and heavy downpours. Boaters should seek safe
harbor immediately until hazardous weather passes.</instruction>
